<title>JAPAN: IBM may launch dual-currency samurais soon.</title>
<headline>IBM may launch dual-currency samurais soon.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp (IBM) is considering launching dual-currency samurai bonds in the near future, underwriting sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They said IBM may launch about 50 billion yen worth of samurai bonds in either yen/Australian dollar denominations or yen/U.S. dollars. The launch date would depend on market conditions, the sources said.</p>
<p>A major Japanese brokerage is expected to lead-manage the issue, they said.</p>
<p>In early September, IBM launched 50 billion yen worth of 5.3 percent yen/U.S. dollar dual-currency samurais.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
